    <h2>What this page could not verify<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="warn">
      Four things, so you know exactly which parts of this page are reads and which are gaps.
      <br><br>
      <b>1. The scribbled note.</b> This is the level's real puzzle and we could not read it. Characters are visible through the scribble, but three separate 4x crops from three different frames produced three different transcriptions, which means none of them is trustworthy. If you solve it with the Ring with numbers, you know something this page does not.
      <br><br>
      <b>2. What the Ring with numbers decodes.</b> The item exists and its label is confirmed at 1:08. It is never used in the recording, so we cannot tell you which prop it points at — we assume the note, and we have not printed that as fact.
      <br><br>
      <b>3. The fifth bottle label.</b> Four of the five labels read cleanly (CARA, ICO, ANTARES, PANIAN). The fifth OCRs as CHT ALE across frames and we could not settle whether that is a real name, so we have not put it in the guide as one.
      <br><br>
      <b>4. The bottles and the glass of water.</b> Both are handled in the run and neither produces anything visible. We do not know whether they are a puzzle that was abandoned mid-run or pure decoration, and we have not invented a purpose for them.
